IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc8-part7-houses.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART VII (Disorderly Houses, Gaming and Betting):
-- section 197 (definitions for this Part), section 199 (search), sections 201 to 203 (keeping a gaming or betting house, betting offences).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The French equivalents in parentheses after a defined term are not text to encode and are quoted only because the quotation is a whole line.
--
-- READING A RESULT. A decision function answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   JUST TRUE    the facts bring the case within the provision on its own words;
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if" / "while" / "only if" / "until" condition, a flat negative);
--   NOTHING      not covered: the text lists without closing the list, says "includes", leaves a term undefined, is silent,
--                points outside the sources, or limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit.
-- An offence provision ("Every one who X is guilty of ...") answers JUST TRUE when X is met and NOTHING when it is not (limited by its own wording):
-- see NOTES.md, Marginal readings for a lawyer, M1. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every offence section has the same three answers: `the person commits the offence` (MAYBE BOOLEAN), `the class of the offence` (Class of offence) and
-- `the punishment` (a LIST OF Punishment, one per limb; a limb that says only "punishable on summary conviction" takes its penalty from the seam
-- input `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`, because section 787 is outside this part).
-- Part-wide seams taken as inputs: `s 2 ...` answers (ccc-definitions) and `s 787(1)` (ccc29). Nothing here is ever a number from memory.

§ `Section 197 -- Interpretation: definitions for Part VII`

-- src:4123 | bet means a bet that is placed on any contingency or event that is to take place in or out of Canada, and without restricting the generality of the foregoing, includes a bet that is placed on any contingency relating to a horse-race, fight, match or sporting event that is to take place in or out of Canada; (pari)
@ref s 197(1) "bet" (src:4123-4123)
GIVEN `it is a bet that is placed on any contingency or event that is to take place in or out of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a bet that is placed on any contingency relating to a horse-race, fight, match or sporting event that is to take place in or out of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) bet` MEANS
    IF `it is a bet that is placed on any contingency or event that is to take place in or out of Canada`
       OR `it is a bet that is placed on any contingency relating to a horse-race, fight, match or sporting event that is to take place in or out of Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "bet means a bet that is placed on any contingency or event that is to take place in or out of Canada"

-- src:4125 | common betting house means a place that is opened, kept or used for the purpose of
-- src:4126 | (a) enabling, encouraging or assisting persons who resort thereto to bet between themselves or with the keeper, or
-- src:4127 | (b) enabling any person to receive, record, register, transmit or pay bets or to announce the results of betting; (maison de pari)
@ref s 197(1) "common betting house" (src:4125-4127)
GIVEN `it is a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is opened, kept or used for the purpose of enabling, encouraging or assisting persons who resort to it to bet between themselves or with the keeper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is opened, kept or used for the purpose of enabling any person to receive, record, register, transmit or pay bets or to announce the results of betting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) common betting house` MEANS
    IF `it is a place`
       AND (   `it is opened, kept or used for the purpose of enabling, encouraging or assisting persons who resort to it to bet between themselves or with the keeper`
            OR `it is opened, kept or used for the purpose of enabling any person to receive, record, register, transmit or pay bets or to announce the results of betting`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "common betting house means a place that is opened, kept or used for the purpose of"

-- src:4128 | common gaming house means a place that is
-- src:4129 | (a) kept for gain to which persons resort for the purpose of playing games, or
-- src:4130 | (b) kept or used for the purpose of playing games
-- src:4131 | (i) in which a bank is kept by one or more but not all of the players,
-- src:4132 | (ii) in which all or any portion of the bets on or proceeds from a game is paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of the place,
-- src:4133 | (iii) in which, directly or indirectly, a fee is charged to or paid by the players for the privilege of playing or participating in a game or using gaming equipment, or
-- src:4134 | (iv) in which the chances of winning are not equally favourable to all persons who play the game, including the person, if any, who conducts the game; (maison de jeu)
@ref s 197(1) "common gaming house" (src:4128-4134)
GIVEN `it is a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is kept for gain to which persons resort for the purpose of playing games` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is kept or used for the purpose of playing games` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in those games a bank is kept by one or more but not all of the players` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in those games all or any portion of the bets on or proceeds from a game is paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in those games, directly or indirectly, a fee is charged to or paid by the players for the privilege of playing or participating in a game or using gaming equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in those games the chances of winning are not equally favourable to all persons who play the game, including the person, if any, who conducts the game` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception in subsection 197(2) applies, by s 197(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) common gaming house` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is a place`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "common gaming house means a place that is"
        IF `it is kept or used for the purpose of playing games`
           AND (   `in those games a bank is kept by one or more but not all of the players`
                OR `in those games the chances of winning are not equally favourable to all persons who play the game, including the person, if any, who conducts the game`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `limbs the exception can reach` AND `the exception in subsection 197(2) applies, by s 197(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `limbs the exception can reach` AND `the exception in subsection 197(2) applies, by s 197(2)` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of subsection 197(2) is itself not covered
        IF `limbs the exception can reach`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A place is not a common gaming house within the meaning of paragraph (a) or subparagraph (b)(ii) or (iii)"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "common gaming house means a place that is"
    WHERE
        -- paragraph (a), or paragraph (b) with subparagraph (ii) or (iii): the only limbs subsection (2) can displace
        `limbs the exception can reach` MEANS
               `it is kept for gain to which persons resort for the purpose of playing games`
            OR (    `it is kept or used for the purpose of playing games`
                AND (   `in those games all or any portion of the bets on or proceeds from a game is paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of the place`
                     OR `in those games, directly or indirectly, a fee is charged to or paid by the players for the privilege of playing or participating in a game or using gaming equipment`))

-- src:4135 | disorderly house means a common betting house or a common gaming house; (maison de désordre)
@ref s 197(1) "disorderly house" (src:4135-4135)
GIVEN `it is a common betting house, by s 197(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a common gaming house, by s 197(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) disorderly house` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a common betting house, by s 197(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `it is a common gaming house, by s 197(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is a common betting house, by s 197(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `it is a common gaming house, by s 197(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "disorderly house means a common betting house or a common gaming house"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): one of the two defined terms is itself not covered

-- src:4136 | game means a game of chance or mixed chance and skill; (jeu)
@ref s 197(1) "game" (src:4136-4136)
GIVEN `it is a game of chance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a game of mixed chance and skill` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) game` MEANS
    IF `it is a game of chance` OR `it is a game of mixed chance and skill`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "game means a game of chance or mixed chance and skill"

-- src:4137 | gaming equipment means anything that is or may be used for the purpose of playing games or for betting; (matériel de jeu)
@ref s 197(1) "gaming equipment" (src:4137-4137)
GIVEN `it is or may be used for the purpose of playing games` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is or may be used for betting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) gaming equipment` MEANS
    IF `it is or may be used for the purpose of playing games` OR `it is or may be used for betting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "gaming equipment means anything that is or may be used for the purpose of playing games or for betting"

-- src:4138 | keeper includes a person who
-- src:4139 | (a) is an owner or occupier of a place,
-- src:4140 | (b) assists or acts on behalf of an owner or occupier of a place,
-- src:4141 | (c) appears to be, or to assist or act on behalf of an owner or occupier of a place,
-- src:4142 | (d) has the care or management of a place, or
-- src:4143 | (e) uses a place permanently or temporarily, with or without the consent of the owner or occupier thereof; (tenancier)
@ref s 197(1) "keeper" (src:4138-4143)
GIVEN `the person is an owner or occupier of a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person assists or acts on behalf of an owner or occupier of a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appears to be, or to assist or act on behalf of an owner or occupier of a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the care or management of a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses a place permanently or temporarily, with or without the consent of the owner or occupier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) keeper` MEANS
    IF     `the person is an owner or occupier of a place`
        OR `the person assists or acts on behalf of an owner or occupier of a place`
        OR `the person appears to be, or to assist or act on behalf of an owner or occupier of a place`
        OR `the person has the care or management of a place`
        OR `the person uses a place permanently or temporarily, with or without the consent of the owner or occupier`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "keeper includes a person who"

-- src:4144 | place includes any place, whether or not
-- src:4145 | (a) it is covered or enclosed,
-- src:4146 | (b) it is used permanently or temporarily, or
-- src:4147 | (c) any person has an exclusive right of user with respect to it; (local ou endroit)
@ref s 197(1) "place" (src:4144-4147)
-- "whether or not (a) it is covered or enclosed, (b) it is used permanently or temporarily, or (c) any person has an exclusive right of user":
-- these three facts make no difference, so the function takes none of them: its answer is the same on every combination (tested).
GIVEN `it is any place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) place` MEANS
    IF `it is any place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "place includes any place"

-- src:4149 | public place includes any place to which the public have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied. (endroit public)
@ref s 197(1) "public place" (src:4149-4149)
GIVEN `the public have access to it as of right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public have access to it by invitation, express or implied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) the place is a public place` MEANS
    IF `the public have access to it as of right` OR `the public have access to it by invitation, express or implied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "public place includes any place to which the public have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied"

-- The seam name that PLAN.md section 6 (ccc10 asks ccc8) gives for the answer subsection 286.1(5) takes from here: the same function under that name.
-- src:4149 | public place includes any place to which the public have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied. (endroit public)
@ref s 197(1) "public place" (seam name of PLAN.md) (src:4149-4149)
GIVEN `the public have access to it as of right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public have access to it by invitation, express or implied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) the place is a place; the place is a public place` MEANS
    `s 197(1) the place is a public place` `the public have access to it as of right` `the public have access to it by invitation, express or implied`

-- src:4151 | (2) A place is not a common gaming house within the meaning of paragraph (a) or subparagraph (b)(ii) or (iii) of the definition common gaming house in subsection (1) while it is occupied and used by an incorporated genuine social club or branch thereof, if
-- src:4152 | (a) the whole or any portion of the bets on or proceeds from games played therein is not directly or indirectly paid to the keeper thereof; and
-- src:4153 | (b) no fee is charged to persons for the right or privilege of participating in the games played therein other than under the authority of and in accordance with the terms of a licence issued by the Attorney General of the province in which the place is situated or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Attorney General thereof.
@ref s 197(2) (src:4151-4153)
GIVEN `it is occupied and used by an incorporated genuine social club or branch of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the whole or any portion of the bets on or proceeds from games played in it is paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a fee is charged to persons for the right or privilege of participating in the games played in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that fee is charged under the authority of and in accordance with the terms of a licence issued by the Attorney General of the province in which the place is situated or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Attorney General thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(2) the place is not a common gaming house within paragraph (a) or subparagraph (b)(ii) or (iii) of the definition` MEANS
    IF     `it is occupied and used by an incorporated genuine social club or branch of one`
       AND (NOT `the whole or any portion of the bets on or proceeds from games played in it is paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of it`)
       AND (   (NOT `a fee is charged to persons for the right or privilege of participating in the games played in it`)
            OR `that fee is charged under the authority of and in accordance with the terms of a licence issued by the Attorney General of the province in which the place is situated or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Attorney General thereof`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while it is occupied and used by an incorporated genuine social club or branch thereof, if" (the exception applies only on those conditions; marginal reading M2)

-- src:4155 | (3) The onus of proving that, by virtue of subsection (2), a place is not a common gaming house is on the accused.
@ref s 197(3) (src:4155-4155)
GIVETH A Party
`s 197(3) the party who bears the onus of proving the exception in subsection 197(2)` MEANS `the accused`

-- src:4157 | (4) A place may be a common gaming house notwithstanding that
-- src:4158 | (a) it is used for the purpose of playing part of a game and another part of the game is played elsewhere;
-- src:4159 | (b) the stake that is played for is in some other place; or
-- src:4160 | (c) it is used on only one occasion in the manner described in paragraph (b) of the definition common gaming house in subsection (1), if the keeper or any person acting on behalf of or in concert with the keeper has used another place on another occasion in the manner described in that paragraph.
@ref s 197(4) (src:4157-4160)
GIVEN `it is used for the purpose of playing part of a game and another part of the game is played elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stake that is played for is in some other place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used on only one occasion in the manner described in paragraph (b) of the definition common gaming house in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the keeper or any person acting on behalf of or in concert with the keeper has used another place on another occasion in the manner described in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(4) the circumstance does not prevent the place from being a common gaming house` MEANS
    IF     `it is used for the purpose of playing part of a game and another part of the game is played elsewhere`
        OR `the stake that is played for is in some other place`
        OR (    `it is used on only one occasion in the manner described in paragraph (b) of the definition common gaming house in subsection (1)`
            AND `the keeper or any person acting on behalf of or in concert with the keeper has used another place on another occasion in the manner described in that paragraph`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A place may be a common gaming house notwithstanding that" (a "may": the text says what does not prevent it, not what does)

§ `Section 199 -- Search`

-- src:4167 | 199 (1) A justice who is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence under section 201, 202, 203, 206 or 207 is being committed at any place within the jurisdiction of the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to enter and search the place by day or night and seize anything found in that place that may be evidence that an offence under section 201, 202, 203, 206 or 207, as the case may be, is being committed at that place, and to take into custody all persons who are found in or at that place and requiring those persons and things to be brought before that justice or before another justice having jurisdiction, to be dealt with according to law.
@ref s 199(1) (src:4167-4167)
GIVEN `the offence is the one the information on oath names` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a justice is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the offence is being committed at a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is within the jurisdiction of the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(1) a justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to enter and search the place` MEANS
    IF     elem (`the offence is the one the information on oath names`'s `section`) (LIST 201, 202, 203, 206, 207)
       AND `a justice is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the offence is being committed at a place`
       AND `the place is within the jurisdiction of the justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may issue a warrant" for "an offence under section 201, 202, 203, 206 or 207 ... at any place within the jurisdiction of the justice"


@ref s 199(1) (the warrant, as against a person found in or at the place) (src:4167-4167)
GIVEN `a warrant has been issued under subsection 199(1) for the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is found in or at the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(1) the warrant authorizes the taking of the person into custody` MEANS
    IF `a warrant has been issued under subsection 199(1) for the place` AND `the person is found in or at the place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all persons who are found in or at that place"

-- src:4169 | (2) A peace officer may, whether or not he is acting under a warrant issued pursuant to this section, take into custody any person whom he finds keeping a common gaming house and any person whom he finds therein, and may seize anything that may be evidence that such an offence is being committed and shall bring those persons and things before a justice having jurisdiction, to be dealt with according to law.
@ref s 199(2) (src:4169-4169)
GIVEN `the person taking into custody is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the place is a common gaming house, by s 197(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer finds the person keeping the common gaming house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer finds the person in the common gaming house` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(2) the peace officer may take the person into custody without a warrant` MEANS
    IF     `the person taking into custody is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the place is a common gaming house, by s 197(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (`the officer finds the person keeping the common gaming house` OR `the officer finds the person in the common gaming house`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, whether or not he is acting under a warrant ... take into custody any person whom he finds keeping a common gaming house and any person whom he finds therein"

@ref s 199(2) (seizure of evidence) (src:4169-4169)
GIVEN `the person seizing is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing may be evidence that an offence of keeping a common gaming house is being committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(2) the peace officer may seize the thing` MEANS
    IF `the person seizing is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the thing may be evidence that an offence of keeping a common gaming house is being committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may seize anything that may be evidence that such an offence is being committed"

-- src:4169 | (2) A peace officer may, whether or not he is acting under a warrant issued pursuant to this section, take into custody any person whom he finds keeping a common gaming house and any person whom he finds therein, and may seize anything that may be evidence that such an offence is being committed and shall bring those persons and things before a justice having jurisdiction, to be dealt with according to law.
@ref s 199(2) (the duty to bring the persons and things before a justice) (src:4169-4169)
DECLARE `s 199(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 199(2) bring the persons and things before a justice having jurisdiction`

@ref s 199(2) (the duty to bring the persons and things before a justice) (src:4169-4169)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 199(2) act`
`s 199(2) the peace officer's duty` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `s 199(2) bring the persons and things before a justice having jurisdiction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a peace officer` BECAUSE "s 199(2): the peace officer did not bring the persons and things before a justice having jurisdiction"

-- The duty as a decision function (the DEONTIC above cannot be compared with EQUALS, so the assertions are made on this twin). No time limit is stated, so none is invented.
@ref s 199(2) (the duty, as a decision function) (src:4169-4169)
GIVEN `the peace officer has taken a person into custody, or seized a thing, under subsection 199(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(2) the peace officer shall bring the persons and things before a justice having jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the peace officer has taken a person into custody, or seized a thing, under subsection 199(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall bring those persons and things before a justice having jurisdiction" (a duty that arises on the custody or seizure)

-- src:4171 | (3) Except where otherwise expressly provided by law, a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom anything that is seized under this section is brought may declare that the thing is forfeited, in which case it shall be disposed of or dealt with as the Attorney General may direct if no person shows sufficient cause why it should not be forfeited.
@ref s 199(3) (src:4171-4171)
GIVEN `the thing was seized under section 199` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing has been brought before a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law otherwise expressly provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(3) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may declare the thing forfeited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the law otherwise expressly provides` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
        IF `the thing was seized under section 199` AND `the thing has been brought before a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom anything that is seized under this section is brought may declare that the thing is forfeited"

@ref s 199(3) (disposal) (src:4171-4171)
GIVEN `the thing has been declared forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person shows sufficient cause why it should not be forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(3) the forfeited thing shall be disposed of or dealt with as the Attorney General may direct` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing has been declared forfeited` AND `a person shows sufficient cause why it should not be forfeited` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no person shows sufficient cause why it should not be forfeited" (marginal reading M2)
        IF `the thing has been declared forfeited` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in which case it shall be disposed of or dealt with" (a consequence of a declaration of forfeiture)

-- src:4175 | (b) the expiration of thirty days from the time of seizure where it is not required as evidence in any proceedings.
@ref s 199(4)(b) (src:4175-4175)
GIVEN `the date of seizure` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the declaration or direction is to be made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(4)(b) thirty days from the time of seizure have expired` MEANS
    -- Fork F1: the thirty days run from the day of seizure; the first day is excluded and the last included (the general rule of counting days, which is outside this text),
    -- so the period ends with day 30 and expires at the end of it: a declaration may be made from day 31.
    IF `the date on which the declaration or direction is to be made` AT LEAST `the date of seizure` PLUS 31
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the expiration of thirty days from the time of seizure" (a period the text fixes in its own words)

-- src:4173 | (4) No declaration or direction shall be made pursuant to subsection (3) in respect of anything seized under this section until
-- src:4174 | (a) it is no longer required as evidence in any proceedings that are instituted pursuant to the seizure; or
-- src:4175 | (b) the expiration of thirty days from the time of seizure where it is not required as evidence in any proceedings.
@ref s 199(4) (src:4173-4175)
GIVEN `it is no longer required as evidence in any proceedings that are instituted pursuant to the seizure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `thirty days from the time of seizure have expired, by s 199(4)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is not required as evidence in any proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(4) a declaration or direction may be made under subsection 199(3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is no longer required as evidence in any proceedings that are instituted pursuant to the seizure` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `thirty days from the time of seizure have expired, by s 199(4)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it is not required as evidence in any proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `thirty days from the time of seizure have expired, by s 199(4)(b)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of paragraph (b) is itself not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No declaration or direction shall be made pursuant to subsection (3) in respect of anything seized under this section until"

-- src:4177 | (5) The Attorney General may, for the purpose of converting anything forfeited under this section into money, deal with it in all respects as if he were the owner thereof.
@ref s 199(5) (src:4177-4177)
GIVEN `the thing has been forfeited under section 199` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is converting it into money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(5) the Attorney General may deal with the forfeited thing as if he were the owner` MEANS
    IF `the thing has been forfeited under section 199` AND `the purpose is converting it into money`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of converting anything forfeited under this section into money"

-- src:4181 | (7) Subsection (6) does not apply to prohibit the seizure, for use as evidence, of any facility or equipment described in that subsection that is designed or adapted to record a communication.
@ref s 199(7) (src:4181-4181)
GIVEN `the facility or equipment is described in subsection 199(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designed or adapted to record a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seizure is for use as evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(7) subsection 199(6) does not apply to prohibit the seizure` MEANS
    IF `the facility or equipment is described in subsection 199(6)` AND `it is designed or adapted to record a communication` AND `the seizure is for use as evidence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (6) does not apply to prohibit the seizure, for use as evidence, of any facility or equipment described in that subsection that is designed or adapted to record a communication" (the text says when (6) does not prohibit; for other cases subsection (6) itself speaks)

-- src:4179 | (6) Nothing in this section or in section 489 authorizes the seizure, forfeiture or destruction of telephone, telegraph or other communication facilities or equipment that may be evidence of or that may have been used in the commission of an offence under section 201, 202, 203, 206 or 207 and that is owned by a person engaged in providing telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public or forming part of the telephone, telegraph or other communication service or system of that person.
@ref s 199(6) (src:4179-4179)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence under section 201, 202, 203, 206 or 207` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility or equipment is telephone, telegraph or other communication facilities or equipment that may be evidence of or may have been used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is owned by a person engaged in providing telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public or forms part of the service or system of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 199(6) does not apply to prohibit the seizure, by s 199(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(6) this section or section 489 authorizes the seizure, forfeiture or destruction of the equipment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection 199(6) does not apply to prohibit the seizure, by s 199(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (7) says only that the prohibition of (6) does not apply to the seizure, not that the seizure is authorized
        IF `the offence is an offence under section 201, 202, 203, 206 or 207` AND `the facility or equipment is telephone, telegraph or other communication facilities or equipment that may be evidence of or may have been used in the commission of the offence` AND `it is owned by a person engaged in providing telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public or forms part of the service or system of that person`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section or in section 489 authorizes the seizure, forfeiture or destruction of telephone, telegraph or other communication facilities or equipment"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this section ... authorizes" applies only to that equipment, owned or forming part of a communication service

§ `Sections 201 to 203 -- Gaming and betting offences`

--                                              mode                  max imprisonment                                min imprisonment            max fine          min fine
-- src:4189 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
@ref s 201(1)(a) (src:4189-4189)
`s 201(1)(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4188 | 201 (1) Every person who keeps a common gaming house or common betting house is guilty of
-- src:4189 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:4190 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 201(1) (src:4188-4190)
GIVEN `the person keeps the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a common gaming house or common betting house, by s 197(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(1) the person commits the offence of keeping a common gaming house or common betting house` MEANS
    IF `the person keeps the place` AND `the place is a common gaming house or common betting house, by s 197(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who keeps a common gaming house or common betting house is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 201(1) (src:4188-4190)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 201(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 201(1) (src:4188-4190)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 201(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 201(1)(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4192 | (2) Every one who
-- src:4193 | (a) is found, without lawful excuse, in a common gaming house or common betting house, or
-- src:4194 | (b) as owner, landlord, lessor, tenant, occupier or agent, knowingly permits a place to be let or used for the purposes of a common gaming house or common betting house,
-- src:4195 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:4196 | Betting, pool-selling, book-making, etc.
@ref s 201(2) (src:4192-4196)
GIVEN `the place is a common gaming house or common betting house, by s 197(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is found in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has lawful excuse for being found in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the owner, landlord, lessor, tenant, occupier or agent of a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly permits the place to be let or used for the purposes of a common gaming house or common betting house` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(2) the person commits the offence of being found in, or permitting the use of, a gaming or betting house` MEANS
    IF     `the place is a common gaming house or common betting house, by s 197(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (   (`the person is found in it` AND (NOT `the person has lawful excuse for being found in it`))
            OR (`the person is the owner, landlord, lessor, tenant, occupier or agent of a place` AND `the person knowingly permits the place to be let or used for the purposes of a common gaming house or common betting house`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who (a) is found, without lawful excuse, in a common gaming house or common betting house, or (b) ... knowingly permits" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 201(2) (src:4192-4196)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 201(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 201(2) (src:4192-4196)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 201(2) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4197 | 202 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:4198 | (a) uses or knowingly allows a place under his control to be used for the purpose of recording or registering bets or selling a pool;
-- src:4199 | (b) imports, makes, buys, sells, rents, leases, hires or keeps, exhibits, employs or knowingly allows to be kept, exhibited or employed in any place under his control any device or apparatus for the purpose of recording or registering bets or selling a pool, or any machine or device for gambling or betting;
-- src:4200 | (c) has under his control any money or other property relating to a transaction that is an offence under this section;
-- src:4201 | (d) records or registers bets or sells a pool;
-- src:4202 | (e) engages in book-making or pool-selling, or in the business or occupation of betting, or makes any agreement for the purchase or sale of betting or gaming privileges, or for the purchase or sale of information that is intended to assist in book-making, pool-selling or betting;
-- src:4203 | (f) prints, provides or offers to print or provide information intended for use in connection with book-making, pool-selling or betting on any horse-race, fight, game or sport, whether or not it takes place in or outside Canada or has or has not taken place;
-- src:4204 | (g) imports or brings into Canada any information or writing that is intended or is likely to promote or be of use in gambling, book-making, pool-selling or betting on a horse-race, fight, game or sport, and where this paragraph applies it is immaterial
-- src:4205 | (i) whether the information is published before, during or after the race, fight game or sport, or
-- src:4206 | (ii) whether the race, fight, game or sport takes place in Canada or elsewhere,
-- src:4207 | but this paragraph does not apply to a newspaper, magazine or other periodical published in good faith primarily for a purpose other than the publication of such information;
-- src:4208 | (h) advertises, prints, publishes, exhibits, posts up, or otherwise gives notice of any offer, invitation or inducement to bet on, to guess or to foretell the result of a contest, or a result of or contingency relating to any contest;
-- src:4209 | (i) wilfully and knowingly sends, transmits, delivers or receives any message that conveys any information relating to book-making, pool-selling, betting or wagering, or that is intended to assist in book-making, pool-selling, betting or wagering; or
-- src:4210 | (j) aids or assists in any manner in anything that is an offence under this section.
@ref s 202(1) (src:4197-4210)
DECLARE `s 202(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 202(1)(a) uses or knowingly allows a place under his control to be used for the purpose of recording or registering bets or selling a pool`
    `s 202(1)(b) imports, makes, buys, sells, rents, leases, hires or keeps, exhibits, employs or knowingly allows to be kept, exhibited or employed in any place under his control any device or apparatus for the purpose of recording or registering bets or selling a pool, or any machine or device for gambling or betting`
    `s 202(1)(c) has under his control any money or other property relating to a transaction that is an offence under this section`
    `s 202(1)(d) records or registers bets or sells a pool`
    `s 202(1)(e) engages in book-making or pool-selling, or in the business or occupation of betting, or makes any agreement for the purchase or sale of betting or gaming privileges, or for the purchase or sale of information that is intended to assist in book-making, pool-selling or betting`
    `s 202(1)(f) prints, provides or offers to print or provide information intended for use in connection with book-making, pool-selling or betting on any horse-race, fight, game or sport`
    `s 202(1)(g) imports or brings into Canada any information or writing that is intended or is likely to promote or be of use in gambling, book-making, pool-selling or betting on a horse-race, fight, game or sport`
    `s 202(1)(h) advertises, prints, publishes, exhibits, posts up, or otherwise gives notice of any offer, invitation or inducement to bet on, to guess or to foretell the result of a contest, or a result of or contingency relating to any contest`
    `s 202(1)(i) wilfully and knowingly sends, transmits, delivers or receives any message that conveys any information relating to book-making, pool-selling, betting or wagering, or that is intended to assist in book-making, pool-selling, betting or wagering`
    `s 202(1)(j) aids or assists in any manner in anything that is an offence under this section`

@ref s 202(1) (src:4197-4210)
GIVEN act IS A `s 202(1) act`
      `it is a newspaper, magazine or other periodical published in good faith primarily for a purpose other than the publication of such information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 202(1)(g) imports or brings into Canada any information or writing that is intended or is likely to promote or be of use in gambling, book-making, pool-selling or betting on a horse-race, fight, game or sport`
        THEN IF `it is a newspaper, magazine or other periodical published in good faith primarily for a purpose other than the publication of such information`
             THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but this paragraph does not apply to a newspaper, magazine or other periodical published in good faith primarily for a purpose other than the publication of such information"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- the act is one of paragraphs (a) to (f), (h), (i) or (j): "Every one commits an offence who"

@ref s 202(1) (src:4197-4210)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 202(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:4213 | (a) for a first offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years;
@ref s 202(2)(a) (src:4213-4213)
`s 202(2)(a) the limb for a first offence` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4214 | (b) for a second offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than fourteen days; and
@ref s 202(2)(b) (src:4214-4214)
`s 202(2)(b) fourteen days` MEANS `Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE

@ref s 202(2)(b) (src:4214-4214)
`s 202(2)(b) the limb for a second offence` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 202(2)(b) fourteen days`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4215 | (c) for each subsequent offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than three months.
@ref s 202(2)(c) (src:4215-4215)
`s 202(2)(c) three months` MEANS `Length of time` OF 0, 3, 0, FALSE

@ref s 202(2)(c) (src:4215-4215)
`s 202(2)(c) the limb for each subsequent offence` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 202(2)(c) three months`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4212 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under this section is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:4213 | (a) for a first offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years;
-- src:4214 | (b) for a second offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than fourteen days; and
-- src:4215 | (c) for each subsequent offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than three months.
@ref s 202(2) (src:4212-4215)
-- Fork F2: "a second offence" and "each subsequent offence" are read by counting the person's earlier CONVICTIONS under this section (one earlier conviction: second; two or more: subsequent).
-- The text does not say whether an earlier offence must have been convicted; the other reading counts earlier offences committed.
GIVEN `the number of earlier convictions of the person for an offence under section 202` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 202(2) the punishment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of earlier convictions of the person for an offence under section 202` EQUALS 0 THEN LIST `s 202(2)(a) the limb for a first offence`
        IF `the number of earlier convictions of the person for an offence under section 202` EQUALS 1 THEN LIST `s 202(2)(b) the limb for a second offence`
        OTHERWISE LIST `s 202(2)(c) the limb for each subsequent offence`

-- src:4217 | 203 Every one who
-- src:4218 | (a) places or offers or agrees to place a bet on behalf of another person for a consideration paid or to be paid by or on behalf of that other person,
-- src:4219 | (b) engages in the business or practice of placing or agreeing to place bets on behalf of other persons, whether for a consideration or otherwise, or
-- src:4220 | (c) holds himself out or allows himself to be held out as engaging in the business or practice of placing or agreeing to place bets on behalf of other persons, whether for a consideration or otherwise,
-- src:4221 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:4222 | (d) for a first offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years,
-- src:4223 | (e) for a second offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than fourteen days, and
-- src:4224 | (f) for each subsequent offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than three months.
@ref s 203 (src:4217-4224)
DECLARE `s 203 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 203(a) places or offers or agrees to place a bet on behalf of another person for a consideration paid or to be paid by or on behalf of that other person`
    `s 203(b) engages in the business or practice of placing or agreeing to place bets on behalf of other persons, whether for a consideration or otherwise`
    `s 203(c) holds himself out or allows himself to be held out as engaging in the business or practice of placing or agreeing to place bets on behalf of other persons, whether for a consideration or otherwise`

@ref s 203 (src:4217-4224)
GIVEN act IS A `s 203 act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203 the person commits the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 203(a) places or offers or agrees to place a bet on behalf of another person for a consideration paid or to be paid by or on behalf of that other person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 203(b) engages in the business or practice of placing or agreeing to place bets on behalf of other persons, whether for a consideration or otherwise` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 203(c) holds himself out or allows himself to be held out as engaging in the business or practice of placing or agreeing to place bets on behalf of other persons, whether for a consideration or otherwise` THEN JUST TRUE

@ref s 203 (src:4217-4224)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 203 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:4223 | (e) for a second offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than fourteen days, and
@ref s 203(e) (src:4223-4223)
`s 203(e) fourteen days` MEANS `Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE

-- src:4224 | (f) for each subsequent offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than three months.
@ref s 203(f) (src:4224-4224)
`s 203(f) three months` MEANS `Length of time` OF 0, 3, 0, FALSE

-- src:4221 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:4222 | (d) for a first offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years,
-- src:4223 | (e) for a second offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than fourteen days, and
-- src:4224 | (f) for each subsequent offence, to imprisonment for not more than two years and not less than three months.
@ref s 203 (src:4221-4224)
-- Fork F2 applies here too (earlier convictions under this section).
GIVEN `the number of earlier convictions of the person for an offence under section 203` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 203 the punishment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of earlier convictions of the person for an offence under section 203` EQUALS 0
        THEN LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (d) a first offence
        IF `the number of earlier convictions of the person for an offence under section 203` EQUALS 1
        THEN LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 203(e) fourteen days`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (e) a second offence
        OTHERWISE LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 203(f) three months`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (f) each subsequent offence
